I pull my suitcase up the stairs.
There is no elevator here.
The suitcase is very heavy.
A woman comes down the stairs.
She has a small dog.
"Good evening, my name is Sabine Krüger," says the woman.
"And this is Bruno," she says and points to the dog.
"Good evening, Frau Krüger," I answer.
"Are you the new tenant?" she asks.
"What is your name?"
"My name is Maya Flores."
"And yes, I am the new tenant," I say.
"Where do you come from, Frau Flores?" asks Frau Krüger.
"I come from Mexico," I answer.
"Oh, from Mexico!"
"Welcome to Berlin," she says warmly.
Bruno sniffs at my suitcase.
"He is very sweet," I say.
"Yes, he is a good dog," says Frau Krüger.
"I wish you a nice evening, Frau Flores," she then says.
"Thank you very much, to you too," I answer.
Frau Krüger and Bruno continue down the stairs.
I take my suitcase and walk to my flat.
